// Benign-but-suspicious pattern: Defender investigating itself — Lab 03
//
// Within minutes of onboarding, DeviceProcessEvents shows signed PowerShell
// launched as SYSTEM by senseir.exe (the MDE live-response / automated-
// investigation sensor) from a DataCollection path. It has the shape of
// PowerShell abuse — but it is Defender's own automated collection.
//
// A PowerShell-abuse detection built on this data WILL false-positive on it
// unless excluded. The discriminators are all three of:
//   - InitiatingProcessFileName == senseir.exe
//   - AccountName == system
//   - -ExecutionPolicy AllSigned in the command line
//   - a "\Windows Defender Advanced Threat Protection\DataCollection\" path
//
// This query ISOLATES the pattern so you can eyeball it. In a real detection,
// invert the final filters to EXCLUDE it.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where DeviceName startswith "lab-win11"     // adjust to your device
| where FileName =~ "powershell.exe"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "senseir.exe"
| where AccountName == "system"
| where ProcessCommandLine has "AllSigned"
   and ProcessCommandLine has @"Windows Defender Advanced Threat Protection\DataCollection"
| project Timestamp, AccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName, ProcessCommandLine
| order by Timestamp desc
